# libpulse is uninstrumented: TSan does not see what orders the mutexes
# its mainloop thread allocates before another thread locks them, and
# reports pa_mutex_lock itself from the connect wait in init on. Only
# reports through that function are suppressed - a suppression on the
# library as a whole would also hide the driver's callbacks, which run
# under libpulse's frames.
race:pa_mutex_lock
